    power: supply: qcom_smbb: accept gadget-managed USB budgets
    
    Initialize an opted-in USB path at 100 mA before registering its supply.
    Prevent userspace from overriding the gadget-managed limit while
    retaining the internal input-current setter used by the USB consumer.
    
    If suspension is refused because the battery is absent, preserve the USB
    power source at the verified minimum input limit and report the refusal.
    Failed hardware transactions still prevent a claimed limit or suspension.
    
    Carry the provider portion of Timothy Schmidt's a0b13a54ac79 with
    Codex:GPT-6 assistance. The current ChipIdea consumer is a separate
    subsystem dependency. Physical USB timing and current remain unqualified.

